  "result": "Checked the candidates; wrapping up now.\n\n{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#32467\", \"PowerToys#44512\", \"PowerToys#32787\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before: an app list in Awake that keeps the PC awake (optionally with the screen on) while the listed processes run. The main thread is PowerToys#32467. PowerToys#44512 was closed as a duplicate of it. The maintainers haven't committed to building it. They are worried about the cost of polling processes and about Awake becoming too complex. The ticket is still open for votes, so add a thumbs-up and your use case there. Until it ships, Awake can already track one process from the command line with `--pid <process id>`, which keeps the PC awake until that process exits. There is no UI for it and no app list. Awake's CLI docs on Microsoft Learn describe it.\"}",
